# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: cli-option-environment-defaults — an environment variable for the default of every option that sets run state
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: feat-cli-option-environment-defaults
#+DATE: 2026-11-13

* Context

The question that started this (pjb, 2026-11-13): /what is the default of
=--host=, and why can't it be set from the environment?/

- =--host= defaults to =cador= (the headless CAD core). The slot in the
  shared =cli-options= struct is =:mock= (deprecated alias of cador;
  =clautolisp/autolisp-cli/source/options.lisp=), which clautolisp maps to
  cador (=main.lisp=, the HAL-backend constructor). That stale default is
  filed separately: =cli-options-host-default-is-deprecated-mock=.
- No environment variable sets it, in either program.

Coverage today is lopsided:

- *alfe* has a table, =+env-defaults+= in
  =autolisp-front-end/source/cli.lisp=, applied by =apply-env-defaults=
  before argv is parsed (so the command line wins):
  =AUTOLISP_MODE=, =AUTOLISP_BACKEND=, =ALFE_BACKEND_OVERRIDE=,
  =AUTOLISP_DWG=, =AUTOLISP_TEMPLATE=, =AUTOLISP_WORKDIR=,
  =AUTOLISP_KEEP_WORKDIR=, =AUTOLISP_WRITE_WORKDIR_PATH=,
  =AUTOLISP_BOOTSTRAP_PHASE=, =AUTOLISP_WAIT_SECS=,
  =AUTOLISP_READY_WAIT_SECS=. Outside the table: =ALFE_PLUGINS=,
  =ALFE_PLUGIN_PATH=, =ALFE_NO_PLUGINS=, and =AUTOCAD_COM_MODE= /
  =BRICSCAD_COM_MODE= for the =--backend= variant of the CAD backends.
- *clautolisp* has three: =--gui= ← =$CLAUTOLISP_GUI=; =--no-init= ←
  =$AUTOLISP_NO_INIT= / =$CLAUTOLISP_NO_INIT= (=no-init-requested-p=);
  =--no-color= ← =$NO_COLOR=.

So a CI job, a daemon, or a wrapper that cannot (or should not) edit every
command line has no way to choose the dialect, the host, the verbosity, the
encodings or the debugger policy.

* Problem

1. Most state-setting options have no environment default (table below).
2. =+env-defaults+= declares six variables that nothing reads:
   =AUTOLISP_OS=, =AUTOLISP_REMOTE_IO_MODE=, =AUTOCAD_INSTALL=,
   =AUTOCAD_VERSION=, =BRICSCAD_INSTALL=, =BRICSCAD_VERSION=
   (=env-default= is only called for the ten keys in =apply-env-defaults=
   plus =:override=). Its docstring claims the table "is exhaustive"; it is
   a list of names, not a list of behaviours.
3. =AUTOLISP_DWG= is honoured by alfe only, although =--dwg= is a common
   option of both programs: the same variable means something to one and
   nothing to the other.

* Proposal

** Naming and precedence

The rule =--no-init= already follows, generalised:

- =AUTOLISP_<OPTION>= for an option *common* to both programs — one
  vocabulary, read the same way by both.
- =CLAUTOLISP_<OPTION>= / =ALFE_<OPTION>= for an option of one program
  only, *and* as a per-program override of a common one.
- Precedence: *command line > =CLAUTOLISP_X= / =ALFE_X= > =AUTOLISP_X= >
  built-in default.*
- Empty value = unset (as =env-default= already does). An invalid value is a
  usage error (=cli-usage-error=) naming the variable, exactly as
  =AUTOLISP_MODE= is handled today — never silently ignored.
- Boolean variables take =1=, =y=, =yes=, =true=, =on= (the plug-in
  activation vocabulary, =AUTOLISP_EPURE=).

** Variables to add

| Option                                                          | Program    | Variable                                                                                                       | Values                                         | Note                                                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------+------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| =--host=                                                        | both       | =AUTOLISP_HOST=                                                                                                | =cador=, =cadtui=, =nihil=                     | default =cador=                                                                            |
| =--dialect= (+ =--strict= / =--autocad= / =--bricscad= / =--clautolisp= / =--lax=) | both | =AUTOLISP_DIALECT=                                                                                    | any =--list-dialects= name                     | alfe: honoured only for the clautolisp backend (a CAD backend imposes its dialect)         |
| =-q= / =-v= / =-d=                                              | both       | =AUTOLISP_VERBOSITY=                                                                                           | =quiet=, =info=, =verbose=, =debug=            |                                                                                            |
| =-E= / =--encoding=                                             | both       | =AUTOLISP_ENCODING=                                                                                            | encoding name                                  | every situation, like the bare =-E=                                                        |
| =-E<situation>[-<dir>]=                                         | both       | =AUTOLISP_<SITUATION>[_<DIR>]_ENCODING=                                                                        | encoding name                                  | generated from =*encoding-situations*= (13 names: =AUTOLISP_SOURCE_ENCODING=, =AUTOLISP_FILE_WRITE_ENCODING=, =AUTOLISP_TERMINAL_OUT_ENCODING=, …) |
| =-Ereplacement= family                                          | both       | =AUTOLISP_ENCODING_REPLACEMENT=, =AUTOLISP_FILE_WRITE_ENCODING_REPLACEMENT=, =AUTOLISP_TERMINAL_OUT_ENCODING_REPLACEMENT= | one character, =error=, =low-byte=, =best-fit=, =escape= | decide the order against the sysvar seed =$CLAUTOLISPENCODINGREPLACEMENT=          |
| =--dwg=                                                         | clautolisp | the existing =AUTOLISP_DWG=                                                                                    | path                                           | already read by alfe; make clautolisp read it too                                          |
| =--dribble=                                                     | both       | =AUTOLISP_DRIBBLE=                                                                                             | boolean, or FILE                               |                                                                                            |
| =--dribble-interactors=                                         | both       | =AUTOLISP_DRIBBLE_INTERACTORS=                                                                                 | =all= or name list                             |                                                                                            |
| =--dcl=                                                         | clautolisp | =CLAUTOLISP_DCL=                                                                                               | =tui=, =gui=, =auto=                           | sits beside =CLAUTOLISP_GUI=                                                               |
| =--on-error=                                                    | clautolisp | =CLAUTOLISP_ON_ERROR=                                                                                          | =quit=, =debug=, =ignore=                      |                                                                                            |
| =--on-interrupt=                                                | clautolisp | =CLAUTOLISP_ON_INTERRUPT=                                                                                      | =debug=, =ignore=, =quit=                      |                                                                                            |
| =--on-quit=                                                     | clautolisp | =CLAUTOLISP_ON_QUIT=                                                                                           | =debug=, =quit=                                |                                                                                            |
| =--debugger-ui=                                                 | clautolisp | =CLAUTOLISP_DEBUGGER_UI=                                                                                       | =dumb=, =ncurses=, =aldb=                      |                                                                                            |
| =--aldb-listen=                                                 | clautolisp | =CLAUTOLISP_ALDB_LISTEN=                                                                                       | =[HOST:]PORT=                                  | opens a socket: a stray export is a risk — pjb to decide whether to include                |
| =--trace=                                                       | clautolisp | =CLAUTOLISP_TRACE=                                                                                             | boolean                                        |                                                                                            |
| =-O= / =--optimize=                                             | clautolisp | =CLAUTOLISP_OPTIMIZE=                                                                                          | =QUALITY=N,…=                                  |                                                                                            |
| =--cad=                                                         | alfe       | =ALFE_CAD=                                                                                                     | CAD denotation                                 | replaces the dead =AUTOCAD_VERSION= / =BRICSCAD_VERSION= entries                           |
| =--backend= (variant)                                           | alfe       | =ALFE_BACKEND_VARIANT=                                                                                         | =attach=, =launch=, =direct=, =subprocess=     | ranks above =AUTOCAD_COM_MODE= / =BRICSCAD_COM_MODE=; not =AUTOLISP_BACKEND=, which is the backend *kind* |

** Deliberately without a variable

Actions, one-shot queries, per-run inputs/outputs, and the internal
alfe ↔ clautolisp protocol — a stray export of any of them would change what a
run *does*, not how:

=--help=, =--version=, =--list-*=, =--probe-gui=, =--dry-run=,
=--print-command=, =-l=, =-x=, =-i=, =--quit=, =--main=, positional FILEs,
=--attach-pid=, =--compile-plugin=, =--mock-input=, =--result-file=,
=--cad-log=, =--cleanup-report=, =--front-end-bindings=,
=--front-end-action-boundaries=, =--aldb-stdio=.

** Implementation shape

- One table, in =autolisp-cli= (beside =*common-option-specs*=), naming each
  option's variable(s) — ideally a slot on =option-spec= itself, so a new
  option is born with (or explicitly without) its variable, and
  =check-user-visible-documentation= iterates that table instead of a
  hand-kept list. alfe's =+env-defaults+= folds into it; the six dead
  entries are removed (or wired, if pjb wants =AUTOLISP_OS= back).
- Applied before argv parsing, in both programs, through the option's own
  value parser (so the env path and the argv path cannot accept different
  spellings).

** alfe → clautolisp child

The clautolisp that alfe spawns (=--backend subprocess=, =--host cadtui=,
=-i=, …) inherits alfe's environment. =AUTOLISP_X= is read identically by
both, but a =CLAUTOLISP_X= set for the user's own clautolisp runs would
override what alfe resolved. So alfe must pass every resolved value of a
transmitted option on the child's argv (argv beats env), and the
=*clautolisp-option-contract*= / parity table gets a row per variable. The
conformance sandbox, which already clears =AUTOLISP_NO_INIT= /
=ALFE_NO_INIT= / =CLAUTOLISP_NO_INIT=, clears the new ones too.

* Acceptance criteria

- Each variable in the table: a test that it sets the default, a test that
  the command-line option beats it, a test that an invalid value is a usage
  error naming the variable; for the common ones, a test that
  =CLAUTOLISP_X= / =ALFE_X= beats =AUTOLISP_X=.
- alfe direct/subprocess parity rows for the transmitted options with a
  conflicting =CLAUTOLISP_X= in the environment.
- The six unread =+env-defaults+= entries are gone or wired.
- Documentation (AGENTS.md user-visible rule): the /Environment variables/
  chapter of =clautolisp-user-manual.org= and =alfe-user-manual.org=
  (alfe's /Option defaults/ table), both man pages' ENVIRONMENT sections,
  the =--help= texts that name a variable; =make
  check-user-visible-documentation= green; =RELEASE_NOTES.org= entries;
  clautolisp + alfe version bumped together.

* Decisions taken before implementing (pjb, 2026-11-14)

The table above contradicted its own naming rule, and left one row open.
Asked and answered:

1. *Prefix of the shared options alfe forwards* (=--dcl=, =--on-error=,
   =--on-interrupt=, =--on-quit=, =--debugger-ui=, =--dribble[-interactors]=):
   =AUTOLISP_*=, not the =CLAUTOLISP_*= the table showed. They are common
   options; =CLAUTOLISP_*= alone stays for clautolisp's own (=--trace=, =-O=).
2. *Per-program override layer*: KEPT, as filed --
   command line > =CLAUTOLISP_<X>= / =ALFE_<X>= > =AUTOLISP_<X>= > default.
3. *=--aldb-listen=*: gets =AUTOLISP_ALDB_LISTEN=.

* Resolved (clautolisp / alfe 2.4.9, 2026-11-14)

What shipped:

- =clautolisp/autolisp-cli/source/environment.lisp=: the literal table
  =*OPTION-ENVIRONMENT-GROUPS*= (30 shared groups, =TRACE= / =OPTIMIZE= for
  clautolisp, =CAD= / =BACKEND_VARIANT= for alfe: 94 variable names) and
  =APPLY-ENVIRONMENT-DEFAULTS=. Each =option-spec= names its GROUP
  (new slots =environment=, =environment-handler=, =environment-layer-p=);
  the parser records the groups the command line set
  (=cli-options-given-environment-groups=), and the defaults fill only the
  others -- so =--strict= keeps =AUTOLISP_DIALECT= out, =-q= keeps
  =AUTOLISP_VERBOSITY= out (the variable SETS a level; it does not go through
  the additive flag rule), and alfe's =--autocad= keeps =ALFE_CAD= out without
  tripping the backend-conflict check.
- Layered groups: the -E encodings and replacements get their own
  environment tables (=cli-options-environment-situation-encodings= /
  =-encoding-replacements=), consulted after the whole command line, so a bare
  =-E utf-8= beats =AUTOLISP_SOURCE_ENCODING=; =CLAUTOLISP_OPTIMIZE='s pairs
  go before the command line's.
- Variables are read through =*ENVIRONMENT-GETENV*= (tests bind a table; the
  three in-process suites bind an empty one so a developer's own exports do
  not change their results). Empty = unset; an invalid value is a usage error
  naming the variable (exit 64).
- *alfe → clautolisp child*: a clautolisp given =--front-end-bindings=
  (which alfe passes on every real =--backend subprocess= run) reads none of
  the variables. alfe resolves them and forwards the result on the child's
  argv; =ENCODING-REPLACEMENT-OPTION-ARGUMENTS= now forwards the RESOLVED
  policies. No change to alfe's own process environment was needed.
- alfe: =AUTOLISP_DWG= moved from alfe's own table to the shared one (gains
  =ALFE_DWG=); the six never-read entries (=AUTOLISP_OS=,
  =AUTOLISP_REMOTE_IO_MODE=, =AUTOCAD_INSTALL=, =AUTOCAD_VERSION=,
  =BRICSCAD_INSTALL=, =BRICSCAD_VERSION=) are gone (the alfe specification
  marks the two it had proposed as not implemented). alfe's other own
  variables (=AUTOLISP_MODE=, =AUTOLISP_WORKDIR=, ...) keep their existing
  mechanism. When a variable makes the run the clautolisp program's
  (=AUTOLISP_HOST=cadtui=, =AUTOLISP_DRIBBLE=, =AUTOLISP_DCL=gui=), the
  =--backend direct= usage error names the variable.
- The conformance sandbox clears every option variable, the list taken from
  the table (=OPTION-ENVIRONMENT-VARIABLE-NAMES=).
- =scripts/check-user-visible-documentation.py= reads the table (the
  getenv-literal scan cannot see composed names); it failed with 119 missing
  names before the manuals were written, and passes after.
- Documentation: clautolisp user manual /Environment variables/ › /Option
  defaults/, alfe user manual /Option defaults/ › /The options alfe shares
  with clautolisp/, both man pages' ENVIRONMENT, the alfe specification,
  RELEASE_NOTES.

Tests: =autolisp-cli/tests/environment-tests.lisp= (table/spec agreement,
precedence, groups, verbosity, encoding layers, replacements, booleans,
optional values, error naming), =tools/clautolisp/tests/environment-option-
tests.lisp= (=CLAUTOLISP_TRACE=, =CLAUTOLISP_OPTIMIZE= layering, dribble,
override, the driven program ignoring the variables), alfe =cli-tests.lisp=
(=ALFE_<X>= over =AUTOLISP_<X>=, =ALFE_CAD= vs a selector,
=ALFE_BACKEND_VARIANT= vs =--attach-pid=, =AUTOLISP_DWG= / =ALFE_DWG=, the
error naming =AUTOLISP_HOST=cadtui=). Checked end to end on the built
clautolisp-sbcl 2.4.9.

Not done here (out of this issue's scope): alfe's pre-seeded =AUTOLISP_BACKEND=
still conflicts with an explicit =--autocad= / =--bricscad= rather than
yielding to it -- see =deferred-alfe-autolisp-backend-yields-to-selector=.
